I think you can get just the third column with

    cut -f 3

from the command line, then pipe it to grep and ID the lines that have the correct value.

So something like

    cut -f 3 | grep 8.9999

but I haven't tried it and I'm probably omitting an important flag.

Hope this helps

Dave

