Hi Erica,

Not sure if it’s the most efficient, but does this work?
apply(m, 1, function(x) {
  if(sum(is.na <http://is.na>(x)) == length(x)) return(NA)
  if(any(x) == 1) return(1)
  0
})

I didn’t test it on your data.frame because it’s hard to copy raw text into a format that r understands. dput(m) is useful for providing data in a way that
​others
can copy right into r.
​

​Hope that helps,

Michael​

​
​

--
Michael Levy
