Interesting.. I've been told repeatedly that they are vectorized and represent a significant time savings, which seems to be borne out by my own experience, but the number of loops I've used where I'm not doing assignment is close to nil.

Some googling suggests that this is actually a big argument. the apply family is usually faster when doing assignment, apparently, but it's complicated:

http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2275896/is-rs-apply-family-more-than-syntactic-sugar

