Seems I have a "solution" to my base problem

| > apply(tw,1,FUN<-function(x,y) {cdef = deparse(substitute(y)); f=parent.env(environment()); p = get(cdef, envir=f); p[x[1],x[2]] = p[x[1],x[2]] + 0.75; assign(cdef,p,envir=f)}, y=j) Of course, this iterates through the lookup table "tw" similar to a loop, rather than keeping a running sum of the changes that need to be made. |

--Matt

