I think Jaime is right.  Mike’s solution seems like an excellent first pass, but it could be tricky to know for sure whether it finds the global optimum unless all the constraints happen to be met on the first try.

My understanding is that this problem falls under the umbrella of integer linear programming <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integer_programming>. There are some packages on the optimization task view <https://cran.r-project.org/web/views/Optimization.html> that are designed for that kind of task, but I don’t know enough about it to translate your problem into an integer program.  If you’re not satisfied with the results from Mike’s approach, finding someone with experience in integer programs or other discrete optimization problems would probably be your best bet.

Hope this helps,

Dave

